Homepage: https://github.com/E-Vex/vted
Description: small, fast terminal text editor for Linux
 vted is a terminal text editor built around one idea: a single C11
 binary with no dependencies beyond the C standard library and POSIX.
 No curses, no plugins, no configuration language - just a fast,
 careful editor that works in any terminal.
 .
 Features: UTF-8 aware editing, incremental search (Ctrl-F), undo and
 redo (Ctrl-Z / Ctrl-Y), auto-indent, whole-line delete and duplicate,
 go-to-line (Ctrl-G) and atomic saves that never lose the original
 file.
 .
 This package ships a statically linked binary, so it runs on any
 glibc or musl based distribution with nothing else to install.
